      "summary": "The tests cover the listed parsing and failure scenarios. The hard memory-limit requirement is not regression-tested on Windows: the 1-byte test can pass through the parent’s sampled check, and the configuration assertion is Linux-only.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/IsolatedPdfParserTests.cs",
          "line": 135,
          "message": "The memory-limit tests do not prove the hard limit is enforced on Windows. Assert the Job Object limit or otherwise make a test fail when that cap is removed.",
          "confidence": 0.95,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "MemoryLimit_KillsWorkerAndReturnsRetryable sets a 1-byte cap and checks only for a retryable result. The parent’s sampled working-set check can produce that result even if the child’s hard memory limit is removed. The only direct limit configuration assertion returns early on non-Linux systems.",
            "failureScenario": "On Windows, remove the Job Object memory cap while retaining the parent’s sampled check. The 1-byte test can still pass when the parent observes the worker’s working set above 1 byte, and the Linux-only assertion is skipped. The suite therefore passes despite removal of the platform’s hard memory limit, contrary to AC-2 and AC-5."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
